{"data": {"event": {"id": "2cf18725-78b1-4522-8d50-f16a7849f416", "picture": "https://services.medicalcongress.online/congress/medias/2026/JFR2026/1899/video/thumbs/poster.jpg", "sessionType": "S\u00e9ance scientifique", "sessionTypeColor": "#44fc54", "voting": null, "title": "S\u00e9ance de communications orales en radioprotection", "start": "2026-10-08T09:00+02:00", "end": "2026-10-08T10:30+02:00", "objectives": ["<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">\u00c0 l\u2019issue de cette session, les participants seront capables de :</p>", "<ol data-spread=\"true\" start=\"1\">", "\t<li><strong>\u00c9valuer les niveaux de dose d\u00e9livr\u00e9s lors des principaux examens et proc\u00e9dures radiologiques</strong>, en s\u2019appuyant sur les niveaux de r\u00e9f\u00e9rence diagnostiques (NRD) et les donn\u00e9es multicentriques disponibles.</li>", "\t<li><strong>Identifier les principaux param\u00e8tres permettant d\u2019optimiser la dose d\u2019irradiation tout en maintenant une qualit\u00e9 d\u2019image diagnostique suffisante</strong>, notamment en scanner et en radiologie interventionnelle.</li>", "\t<li><strong>Comprendre l\u2019apport des nouvelles technologies d\u2019imagerie et des outils de reconstruction avanc\u00e9e</strong> dans l\u2019optimisation du rapport dose/qualit\u00e9 d\u2019image, notamment le comptage photonique, l\u2019imagerie spectrale et l\u2019optimisation de la collimation.</li>", "</ol>"], "onAir": null, "vod": {"checkPermissions": ["media:view"], "media": null}, "broadcasts": {"items": []}, "room": {"id": "12ce8395-2cd0-409b-937e-fb761e888ff4", "name": "253", "type": "ROOM"}, "schedule": {"items": [{"id": "24305374-f6a2-42aa-a9f0-cc4564686618", "title": "Bilan triennal des NRD, sur les donn\u00e9es 2022-2024", "start": "2026-10-08T09:00+02:00", "end": "2026-10-08T09:09+02:00", "element": {"abstract": {"id": "24305374-F6A2-42AA-A9F0-CC4564686618"}}, "speakers": {"items": [{"id": "034eb94b-592a-41ff-982a-74d55742e169", "lastName": "Danvin", "firstName": "